From ir2_a22x Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 18:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: ir2_nir skip A20X memexport CFs for A22X binning

Fork A/B (patch 0093) enabled use_hw_binning() for A22X, wiring the
Mesa batch->binning IB infrastructure to the A22X hw binner. First
test of that change (libgallium md5 cd138bc17bfb) HARD-LOCKED the
device on the first submit — netconsole stopped after submit#1.

Root cause: extra_position_exports() in ir2_nir.c unconditionally
emits 8 memexport CFs into the binning shader variant. These CFs
reference shader constants 3..10 and 67..82 which fd2_gmem.c
populates with VSC pipe BO addresses + clip transforms ONLY in the
A20X branch of use_hw_binning. For A22X we skip those constants
(the hw binner is the actual visibility producer). With the
constants uninitialized, the memexport CFs write to address 0 or
similar invalid memory → GPU MMU fault → hard hang.

Fix: skip the 8 memexport CFs entirely when targeting A22X.

```
if (!binning)
    return;

/* A20X uses shader memexport; A22X uses the HW binner. */
+if (!ctx->so->is_a20x)
+    return;

// existing 8-iteration memexport loop (A20X-only now)
```

The binning shader for A22X is then VS-only with no memexports —
the regular position output goes to SQ_PARAMETER_PIXEL where the
HW binner consumes it.

Companion to 0093 Fork A/B integration. Must be applied to avoid
hard hangs when use_hw_binning returns true for A22X.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/ir2_nir.c
@@ -951,6 +951,19 @@
    if (!binning)
       return;
 
+   /* A20X hw binning emits the visibility stream via 8 shader memexport
+    * CFs (one per VSC pipe). The CFs reference shader constants 3..10 and
+    * 67..82 which fd2_gmem.c populates with pipe BO addresses + clip
+    * transforms in the A20X branch of use_hw_binning.
+    *
+    * A22X uses the hardware binner (engaged via LRZ_VSC_CONTROL=3) which
+    * writes visibility data itself. Emitting these CFs on A22X writes to
+    * undefined memory because the A20X memexport address constants are
+    * skipped. Skip them entirely for A22X binning shaders.
+    */
+   if (!ctx->so->is_a20x)
+      return;
+
    off = instr_create_alu(ctx, nir_op_fadd, 1);
    off->src[0] = ir2_src(64, 0, IR2_SRC_CONST);
    off->src[1] = ir2_src(2, 0, IR2_SRC_INPUT);
